<!--
  Abstract sound-wave motif: three concentric arcs radiating from a small
  source dot, all within the adaptive-icon safe zone (inner 66dp of the
  108dp canvas, i.e. within 33dp of center (54,54)) so round/squircle
  launcher masks never clip it. Deliberately quiet/symmetric (SOUL.md),
  no photorealism.

  Centering (Opus Review Befund 2026-07-12): the arcs open to the right
  and don't bulge left, so the visible motif isn't symmetric around its own
  arc centers; its visible x-range was originally [41, 84] (leftmost:
  dot at cx minus r equals 41; rightmost: outermost arc bulge at cx plus r
  equals 84), midpoint 62.5, i.e. 8.5dp right of the canvas center x=54.
  Shifted the whole group by 8.5dp to the left in x (dot cx 44 to 35.5,
  arc centers 50/53/56 to 41.5/44.5/47.5; y unchanged, already symmetric)
  so the visible range becomes [32.5, 75.5], midpoint 54. Re-verified
  against the safe zone after the shift (farthest point of each shape from
  canvas center (54,54)): dot 21.5dp, arc1 17.33dp, arc2 22.14dp,
  arc3 28.74dp, all still under the 33dp limit.
-->
